# Phuket Harbour — Cursor Rules
# Read this file before editing any code in this project.

## Project Overview
Static single-page website for **Phuket Harbour** — a local Phuket ferry and island tour operator since 1994.

- **Stack**: Vanilla HTML + CSS + JS, single file (`index.html`). No framework, no bundler.
- **Fonts**: Google Fonts — Playfair Display (headings) + Inter (body). Both already loaded.
- **Payment**: Omise.js (`cdn.omise.co/omise.js.gz`) — set `OMISE_PUBLIC_KEY` in the script block.
- **WhatsApp**: Replace ALL instances of `66XXXXXXXXX` with the real Thai mobile number (format: 66XXXXXXXXX, no + or spaces).

## File Structure
```
phuket-harbour/
├── index.html          ← entire site (HTML + CSS + JS, ~1800 lines)
├── assets/
│   ├── videos/         ← 6 background MP4s (Git LFS tracked)
│   │   ├── pexels-maksim-romashkin-12762099 (2160p).mp4
│   │   ├── pexels-silent-sightseer-11720101 (Original).mp4
│   │   ├── production_id_5147338 (1080p).mp4
│   │   ├── pexels-francesco-navarro-6216472 (1080p).mp4
│   │   ├── pexels-ibrahim-bennett-18110059 (2160p).mp4
│   │   └── pexels-maksim-romashkin-12762055 (2160p).mp4
│   └── images/
│       └── logo-white.png  ← white version of logo for nav/footer (place here)
```

## Design Tokens (CSS custom properties in :root)
```
--navy:    #142864   (primary brand navy)
--navy-dk: #0d1a40   (darkest navy, used for hero/footer bg)
--navy-lt: #1e3575   (lighter navy, hover states)
--coral:   #f07850   (primary accent / CTA colour)
--coral-dk:#d4603a   (coral hover)
--coral-lt:#fde8df   (coral tint backgrounds)
--white:   #ffffff
--warm:    #faf9f7   (off-white section backgrounds)
--grey:    #64748b   (body text secondary)
--border:  #e5e9f0
--text:    #1c2240   (dark text)
```

## Key Sections (by HTML id)
| id | Description |
|----|-------------|
| `#nav` | Fixed nav, transparent → darkens on scroll (JS adds `.scrolled` at 80px) |
| `#hero` | Full-screen cycling video hero with inline SVG logo |
| `#book-strip` | Quick booking widget below hero (5-column grid on desktop) |
| `#trust-bar` | 5 trust icons strip |
| `#services` | 6 service cards |
| `#compare` | Price comparison table (navy bg) |
| `#how` | How to book — tabbed (WhatsApp / Online) |
| `#schedule` | Daily schedule — tabbed (Phi Phi / Krabi / Return) |
| `#tour` | Phi Phi full-day tour with timeline |
| `#trust` | About us + trust cards |
| `#reviews` | 6 review cards |
| `#faq` | 8 FAQ items using `<details>`/`<summary>` |
| `#cta` | Navy CTA strip |
| `#wa-float` | Fixed WhatsApp bubble (bottom-right) |
| `#modal-overlay` | 4-step booking modal with Omise payment |

## Hero Videos
- 6 `<video class="hv">` elements inside `.hero-vids`
- JS cycles them with 1.8s CSS opacity crossfade
- First video has `preload="auto" loop`, rest have `preload="none"` (lazy)
- Fallback: if no video loads, hero shows `--navy-dk` solid background

## Booking Modal Flow
1. Select service (data-svc, data-price attributes)
2. Date, adults, children, hotel, contact
3. Card payment via Omise (`processPayment()` → `Omise.createToken()` → `chargeWithToken()`)
4. Success screen with booking reference

`chargeWithToken(tokenId)` is a stub — wire it to your backend endpoint to actually charge.

## Things to Configure Before Going Live
- [ ] Replace `66XXXXXXXXX` with real WhatsApp number (5 occurrences)
- [ ] Replace `pkey_test_YOUR_OMISE_PUBLIC_KEY` with real Omise public key
- [ ] Implement `chargeWithToken()` → POST to your server-side charge endpoint
- [ ] Add `logo-white.png` to `assets/images/`
- [ ] Update canonical URL meta tag (`https://phuket-harbour.com/`)
- [ ] Replace `og:image` meta with a real image URL
- [ ] Update footer social links (Facebook, Instagram, TripAdvisor)

## Coding Rules
- Keep everything in `index.html` — do not split into separate CSS/JS files unless asked
- Use the existing CSS custom properties; do not hardcode colour hex values
- Responsive breakpoints: 1024px (tablet) and 768px (mobile) — both already handled
- All external links must have `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`
- No jQuery, no React, no build tools — plain ES5-compatible JavaScript only
- Keep the Omise `<script>` loading with `defer` — it must be on the page for payment to work
